sage_chars:\n            record = copy.copy(record)\n            record.msg = self._truncate_message(message, self.max_message_chars)\n            record.args = None\n    msg = super().format(record)\n    ...\n```\n\nCareful: original code `msg.find(record.message)`. Since record may be a copy with msg set, record.message will be set by super().format on the copy. Fine.\n\nBut wait, exception text: if record.exc_info and truncated message, super().format appends exception text — preserved, not truncated since we only truncate message. Good.\n\nEdge: record.getMessage() itself does `msg = str(self.msg); if self.args: msg = msg % self.args`. If msg already str but args present. Setting copy.msg to truncated and args None works, though if the truncated message contains '%'... super().format does record.message = record.getMessage() → with args None returns str(msg) — fine.\n\nAlso validation: max_message_chars must be int >= 32, bool excluded. Use:\n\n```python\ndef __init__(self, fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False, *, max_message_chars=None):\n    super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n    if max_message_chars is not None:\n        if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n            raise ValueError(...)\n        if max_message_chars < 32:\n            raise ValueError(...)\n    self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n```\n\n_error message arbitrary.\n\nTruncation: marker = \"...<omitted>...\" length 15. remaining = budget - 15. If remaining < 0? budget >= 32 so remaining >= 17. head = (remaining + 1)//2, tail = remaining - head. text = message[:head] + marker + message[len(message)-tail:] (tail may be 0 → message[-0:] is whole message! Careful: if tail == 0 use \"\" . remaining>=17 so head>=9, tail>=8, non-zero. Fine but guard.\n\nNow _setup_logger: add max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS. Need import envs. Check environ.py imports to avoid circular. Let me read environ.py first 30 lines